As I have it here it actually appears to not be working. Will post back here if I figure it out.

On Monday, November 11, 2019 at 3:08:29 PM UTC-7, Vincent Landau wrote:
> I'm developing a package that depends on nimble. I have a custom distribution that I register with nimble, so I have a script inside of the R/ folder that just has all of those nimbleFunctions defined. Something about them being nimble functions causes covr to ignore those lines of code (if no R functions are in the script, it ignores the script entirely). This results in those lines not being considered in coverage reports (e.g. generated for covr.io <http://covr.io>).
>
> I'm guessing it's much more complicated that it might seem at first glance, but I wanted to flag it here just so devs and others are aware. I did find a hacky workaround that I'll use in the meantime. See the following basic example.
>
> r_function_add <- function(a, b) {
>   return(a + b)
> }
> nimble_function_add <- nimbleFunction(
>   run = function(a = double(1), b = double(1)) {
>     returnType(double(0))
>     return(r_function_add(a, b))
>   }
> )
>
> Then, testthat tests can be run on nimble_function_add() and coverage corresponding to R_function_add() will be reported.

